==============================================================================
LEG 1: known 2-jet Keller maps -- exact field degrees and graded system
==============================================================================
T1 = (x+z^2, y, z): polynomial inverse (P1-P3^2, P2, P3) verified both ways.
    det J = 1, D5..D1 = 0, D0 = 1, box (dA,dB,dC) = (0,0,1). FIELD DEGREE = 1.
T2 = (xz^2+yz+xy-x^3+x, z^2+3x^2-2y, x+z): NEW EXPLICIT POLYNOMIAL INVERSE
    x = P1 - (P3^3 - P2*P3)/2 ;  z = P3 - x ;  y = ((P3-x)^2 + 3x^2 - P2)/2
    verified both compositions = identity. det J = -2, D5..D1 = 0, D0 = -2.
    box (dA,dB,dC) = (1,1,3). FIELD DEGREE = 1.
W = THM-1310 map: det J = -2, D-system (0,0,0,0,0,-2), B on cusp cone 27B1^2B3+B2^3=0.
    fiber count mod 10007: 3 (0.1s), mod 31013: 3 (0.1s)  -- expected 3
    D0(T2) = D0(W) = -2 with field degrees 1 vs 3: D0 carries NO field-degree info.
D0-consequences verified: ideal(B_W) = (1) [B nowhere 0]; ideal(C2_x x C2_y) = (1)
    [C is an everywhere-immersion for T2]. Both are forced by D0 = const != 0.

==============================================================================
LEG 2: the projected plane fiber system (frame identities, proof-grade)
==============================================================================
Res_z(E_i, E_j) = a_k^2 - u_k b_k  for (i,j,k) cyclic  -- EXACT, 9 generic symbols.
u.A = u.B = 0 and u.C~ = det[A|B|C~] = g1: u = AxB is the LEFT KERNEL of the
fiber matrix on {g1=0}; u_k != 0 makes E_k redundant, so the fiber bijects with
{g1 = 0, g2_k = 0, u_k != 0} via z = a_k/u_k.  (Lemma proof in report.)

